NAME
     file - what kind of file this is

SYNOPSIS
     file [-b] [-i] [-L] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
     file looks at the first bytes of each FILE and says what it appears
     to be: an ELF binary and for what machine, an archive, a
     compressed stream, a script with the interpreter it names, an image
     of a file system, text, or data.

OPTIONS
     -b   the answer alone, without the name in front of it
     -i   a MIME type instead of a sentence
     -L   follow symbolic links

SEE ALSO
     stat(1), strings(1), od(1)
